  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Federal Systems L P reported $1.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 427 awards with an average award size of $2.8M. Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations are down 10.2% year over year. FY21 obligations were $1.6B, FY22 obligations were $1.7B, FY23 obligations were $1.4B, FY24 obligations were $1.5B, and FY25 obligations were $1.3B, showing a multi-year pattern of variation. Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $512M to Dell Federal Systems L P so far in FY2026, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $246M and Department of Health and Human Services at $138M. Software Publishers is the largest market for Dell Federal Systems L P in FY2026 to date, with $953M in obligations, followed by a second Software Publishers entry at $125M and Other Computer Related Services at $59.5M. Dell Federal Systems L P also records obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Storage Device Manufacturing, among smaller NAICS categories. This profile highlights concentration in a few agencies and a dominant software market presence.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations peaked at $1.7B in FY22 and have since moved lower: FY23 obligations were $1.4B, FY24 obligations were $1.5B, FY25 obligations were $1.3B, and FY26 obligations are $1.2B to date. Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations are down 10.2% year over year for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and NAICS markets drive Dell Federal Systems L P's federal work?",
        "body": "Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of Dell Federal Systems L P in FY2026 to date with $512M in obligations, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $246M and Department of Health and Human Services at $138M. Software Publishers is the dominant NAICS market for Dell Federal Systems L P with $953M in obligations, supported by other IT-related markets such as Other Computer Related Services at $59.5M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $52.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
